Prawn Monitor is an original project. Its tank-node and local-hub layout is
inspired by Sync Tank, an MIT-licensed aquarium workshop:

  Sync Tank — https://github.com/looseleif/sync-tank
  Copyright holders as named in that repository
  License: MIT

Prawn Monitor does not copy Sync Tank source code. It does not include Sync
Tank's spatial model, robotic camera rigs, or optional cloud image analysis.

AMADEUS (https://amadeus.jpmyrmecol.com/, https://github.com/jpmyrmecol/AMADEUS)
is a separate program under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only.
Prawn Monitor does not vendor, link, or distribute AMADEUS. It records fixed
overhead clips and imports tracking CSV files that AMADEUS writes.
